# fixedbugs, defect 570, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R1).
#
# SYMPTOM: through a header writing `#pragma clang diagnostic ignored
# "-Wint-conversion"`, `read_p(p: i64)` against `int read_p(int *)` built,
# and `read_p(7)` read through address 7 and aborted 134 at run time.
#
# CAUSE: clang makes `-Wint-conversion` an error by default, no flag of the
# build names it, and the header's pragma turned it off at the probe.
#
# FIX: after the groups' includes, and again at the probe region, every
# warning a check of a binding rests on is raised again
# (`emit/checks_raised.hero`), the build's `-Werror` words and clang's three
# default errors, so the message is the one a plain header gets.

extern "fixedbugs-570-an-integer-for-a-pointer-is-refused-through-the-pragma.h"
    function read_p(p: i64) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    print(read_p(7))
